   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi, Recently I found a solution to trigger an action button on (non-reactive) variable.  </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36671011/action-button-and-observeevent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36671011/action-button-and-observeevent&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388660226000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1aLkdlZixuTDsRf0SvvDyi\">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36671011/action-button-and-observeevent</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>This solution also works with a matrix, but not wirh a data.frame. This is my test code.<br></div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(shiny)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">ui = fluidPage(</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>actionButton(inputId = &quot;action&quot;, label = &quot;action&quot;),</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>#textOutput(&quot;txt_example1&quot;)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>tableOutput(&quot;txt_example1&quot;)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">server = function(input, output) {</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>#rv = reactiveValues( x=c(1,2,3) )</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>rv = reactiveValues( x=matrix(c(1,2,3,4),nrow=2) )</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>#rv = reactiveValuesToList( x=data.frame(matrix(c(1,2,3,4),nrow=2) ))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>observe({</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t</span>#output$txt_example1 = renderText({ rv$x })</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t</span>output$txt_example1 = renderTable({ rv$x })</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>})</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>observeEvent(input$action, {</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t</span>rv$x = rv$x + 1</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>})</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">}</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">shinyApp(ui = ui, server )</font></div></div><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>What could be the best solution?</div><div><br></div><div>Plus, it is possible to use the similar approach  with more complicated R objects? For example:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:21px;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; x</span><span style=\"color:blue\">\r\n</span>#\r\n# Gene Set Enrichment Analysis\r\n#\r\n#...@organism \t human \r\n#...@setType \t Reactome \r\n#...@keytype \t ENTREZID \r\n#...@geneList \t Named num [1:12495] 4.57 4.51 4.42 4.14 3.88 ...\r\n - attr(*, &quot;names&quot;)= chr [1:12495] &quot;4312&quot; &quot;8318&quot; &quot;10874&quot; &quot;55143&quot; ...\r\n#...nPerm \t 1000 \r\n#...pvalues adjusted by &#39;BH&#39; with cutoff &lt;0.2 \r\n#...28 enriched terms found\r\n&#39;data.frame&#39;:\t28 obs. of  8 variables:\r\n $ ID             : chr  &quot;1474244&quot; &quot;913531&quot; &quot;73894&quot; &quot;2555396&quot; ...\r\n $ Description    : Factor w/ 72 levels &quot;Adaptive Immune System&quot;,..: 23 35 16 41 51 40 49 25 2 50 ...\r\n $ setSize        : int  228 166 125 139 130 138 142 159 141 173 ...\r\n $ enrichmentScore: num  -0.446 0.392 0.414 0.661 0.662 ...\r\n $ NES            : num  -1.88 1.71 1.75 2.82 2.8 ...\r\n $ pvalue         : num  0.00141 0.0031 0.00318 0.00326 0.00326 ...\r\n $ p.adjust       : num  0.0193 0.0193 0.0193 0.0193 0.0193 ...\r\n $ qvalues        : num  0.0127 0.0127 0.0127 0.0127 0.0127 ...</font></pre></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I want to process this object in the observeEvent() triggered by actionButton...</font><br></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
